cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "pl-forecast-bench: a leakage-checked forecasting benchmark for the Polish power system"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Waleszczyński"
    given-names: "Konrad"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kwwaleszczynski-del/pl-forecast-bench"
url: "https://kwwaleszczynski-del.github.io/pl-forecast-bench/"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark of day-ahead and intraday (1-6 h) forecasts at 15-minute resolution for national wind generation,
  solar generation, power demand and the SDAC day-ahead price in Poland. It fixes the data (PSE reports, archived
  ECMWF IFS forecasts through Open-Meteo, with download scripts and checksums), the as-of rules (publication times
  of every input), the train/validation/test splits with a 12-month test year, the metrics (MAE, RMSE, nMAE, pinball,
  CRPS, imbalance cost, battery profit) and reference models, and ships tests that detect look-ahead leakage.
keywords:
  - forecasting
  - benchmark
  - wind power
  - solar power
  - electricity demand
  - electricity price
  - Poland
  - time series foundation models
